@title EPISODE 24 • INDOOR SEASON
@bg indoor_training_facility
January. Indoor season. The banked track smells like rubber and new beginnings.
@show holloway
Holloway: Welcome back. Some of you trained over break. Some of you ate. Coach King will be finding out which.
@show coachking
Coach King: Leaderboard's up. If your name's at the bottom, you live in my weight room now.
Caleb's name is at the bottom. Shane pats his back.
@show holloway
Holloway: Distance and sprints are cross-training again. Sterling. Williams. You're partners.
London: Coach. You're doing this on purpose.
Holloway: I do everything on purpose. That's why I'm the head coach.
@show diggy
Diggy: (awkward) Hey.
London: Hey.
@show coachm
Coach M: (from across the track) Okay, Romeo and Juliet, you can be sad AND fast! Drop and give me strides!
> [Bold] "Race me. 300. Like old times." -> r1
> [Sweet] "My dad called your mom. I know. Thank you for telling me first." -> r2
> [Bitchy] "Just do the drill, Williams." -> r3
> [Good] Run the strides in silence, side by side. -> r4
*r1
@add Diggy_Affection 3
Diggy: (grinning for the first time in weeks) Oh, it's ON.
You lose by a step again. You both laugh so hard Coach M has to sit down.
@jump r_done
*r2
@add Diggy_Trust 3
Diggy: She said he apologized for twenty minutes. She made him a plate over the phone. Like, verbally.
@jump r_done
*r3
@add Diggy_Hurt 1
@add Coach_Respect 1
Diggy: (quiet) Okay. Drill.
@jump r_done
*r4
@add Diggy_Trust 2
Eight strides. Step for step. By the last one your arms are swinging in time without either of you trying.
*r_done
@show coachbrooks
Coach Brooks: (handing London a coffee she didn't ask for) For the record, your recovery runs were perfect over break. Don't tell Holloway I noticed. She'll get emotional.
@show holloway
Holloway: I heard that.
